    "## 1. This week's cheat sheet\n",
    "\n",
    "On the **same sheet of paper** you started in Week 1, add your handwritten notes for this week.\n",
    "This week's cheat sheet should contain notes about:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Classes:** `class Name:` defines the shape; `__init__(self, ...)` fills in each new object\n",
    "2. **`self`:** the particular object the method was called on\n",
    "3. **Attributes:** stored with `self.x = x`, read with `obj.x` (a dot, not `[\"key\"]`)\n",
    "4. **Objects are separate:** changing one object does not change another\n",
    "5. **Methods:** `def method(self):` inside the class, called as `obj.method()`; one method can call another with `self.`\n",
    "6. **Methods can change their own object:** e.g. a running count stored on `self`\n",
    "7. **Class-level attributes:** one value shared by every object of the class\n",
    "8. **A list of objects:** loop over it and call a method on each; load it from a file\n",
    "\n",
    "Write them in your own words, with a short example for each. Do not copy from the slides."
