   "source": [
    "### C1. Count the records over the limit\n",
    "\n",
    "Add a method `is_over(self)` to `Record` that returns `True` or `False`. Load `records_sample.txt` with\n",
    "`load_records` from D11, use `is_over()` to count how many records are over their limit, and print a\n",
    "one-line summary.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Expected output:** `1 of 3 records are OVER LIMIT`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 13,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "1 of 3 records are OVER LIMIT\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "class Record:\n",
    "    def __init__(self, label, value, limit):\n",
    "        self.label = label\n",
    "        self.value = value\n",
    "        self.limit = limit\n",
    "\n",
    "    def percent(self):\n",
    "        return self.value / self.limit * 100\n",
    "\n",
    "    def status(self):\n",
    "        p = self.percent()\n",
    "        if p >= 100:\n",
    "            return \"OVER LIMIT\"\n",
    "        if p >= 90:\n",
    "            return \"WARNING\"\n",
    "        return \"OK\"\n",
    "\n",
    "    def is_over(self):\n",
    "        return self.percent() >= 100\n",
    "\n",
    "loaded_records = load_records(\"records_sample.txt\")\n",
    "over_count = sum(record.is_over() for record in loaded_records)\n",
    "print(f\"{over_count} of {len(loaded_records)} records are OVER LIMIT\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### C2. An account that locks\n",
    "\n",
    "Write a class `Account` with a `username` and a count of failed logins that starts at 0.\n",
    "It has two methods:\n",
    "\n",
    "- `fail(self)`: adds 1 to the failed logins\n",
    "- `locked(self)`: returns `True` if there have been 3 or more failed logins\n",
    "\n",
    "**Test it:**\n",
    "\n",
    "| Code | Expected output |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| an account for `\"anna\"` with `.fail()` called 3 times, then `print(anna.locked())` | `True` |\n",
    "| an account for `\"ben\"` with `.fail()` called once, then `print(ben.locked())` | `False` |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 14,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "True\n",
      "False\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "class Account:\n",
    "    def __init__(self, username):\n",
    "        self.username = username\n",
    "        self.failed_logins = 0\n",
    "\n",
    "    def fail(self):\n",
    "        self.failed_logins += 1\n",
    "\n",
    "    def locked(self):\n",
    "          return self.failed_logins >= 3\n",
    "\n",
    "anna = Account(\"anna\")\n",
    "for _ in range(3):\n",
    "    anna.fail()\n",
    "ben = Account(\"ben\")\n",
    "ben.fail()\n",
    "print(anna.locked())  # True\n",
    "print(ben.locked())   # False\n"
   ]
  },
